{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1513372273,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM1MjExMjczOQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2034#issuecomment-352112739"},"message":"If we want to keep git-annex compat, this is the constraint: \"field names are limited to alphanumerics (and [_-.]), and are case insensitive\"","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1513372450,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM1MjExMzMxMg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2034#issuecomment-352113312"},"message":"We need three special characters in the search keys:\n\n- one to separate the name space from the actual key\n- one to go down into a nested property\n- one to replace any occurrence of the above two chars in any incoming key string with","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1517298423,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM2MTUwMzc1MA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2034#issuecomment-361503750"},"message":"This issue is no longer concerned with metadata keys, after the switch to the new layout in #2112. However, we may still want to adopt a common scheme when there is need to flatten a nested metadata structure, e.g. in whoosh-based search index construction (or anything like that).\n\nMaybe like this:\n\n- any occurence of '-' or '.' in a key is replaced by '_'\n- '.' is used when going down a level\n- '-' is the prefix separator (motivated by whoosh's language using the ':' as the field separator already. Hence {bids: {prefix:participant: age: 26}} would come out as 'bids.prefix-participant.age'","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1518255828,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM2NDYzOTQ2NQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datala